{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=-1 \\\\  & x-2y=1 \\\\  & -x-5y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 7y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-\\frac{3}{7}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{3}{7})=1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\n \nSo, we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0652a6da08e87cd730e3a770705b777232b1b034e99a26759e2443c42a3a278b"} {"question" "q-74637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=8 \\\\  & x+y=-2 \\\\  & x+\\frac{1}{2}y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y=-2 \\\\ -y=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-14.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-14)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=12.\n$$\n\n \nSo,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent.   \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0652a6da08e87cd730e3a770705b777232b1b034e99a26759e2443c42a3a278b"} {"question" "q-74643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 4x+2y=-8 \\\\  & x+ky=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & k & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & k & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2-4k & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=2 \\\\  & (2-4k)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{1}{2},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=2.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0652a6da08e87cd730e3a770705b777232b1b034e99a26759e2443c42a3a278b"} {"question" "q-74695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "k=2"] ["math" "k=\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "k=\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "k=\\frac{1}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-74695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+7y=1 \\\\  & -2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent dependent" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131721" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0652a6da08e87cd730e3a770705b777232b1b034e99a26759e2443c42a3a278b"} {"question" "q-131721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131721" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & -3x+2y=1 \\\\  & 6x+(k+9)y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+9 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+9 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k+13 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y=1 \\\\ (k+13)y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=-13,$ then the second equation is $0=7,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=-13.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0652a6da08e87cd730e3a770705b777232b1b034e99a26759e2443c42a3a278b"} {"question" "q-131726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-12"] ["math" "k=-13"] ["math" "k=-14"] ["math" "k=7"] ["math" "k=8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"} {"question" "q-131726" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=-13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14057024/state.json" "file_sha256" "3e9259137f358e0539b35cd2747261c3e4f1c442d5ba5ed3a6de8a66e92d9d9c"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1838 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
